\f0\fs24 \cf0 To get fluoresence graphs from Z-stack. \
\
Open FIJI\
\
File \'97> open file\
\
Select hyper stack and composite but nothing else, ensure autoscale is off\
\
Go to image \'97> color \'97> split channels\
\
Go to a representative z stack and draw a line\
\
Press T to add it to ROI manager\
	If ROI manager goes away can get it in analyze \'97> tools\
\
In the ROI panel go to more \'97> multi measure and select all slices and one row per slice\
\
Go to analyze \'97> plot profile. It will plot the fluorescence over the distance of the line\
\
Data \'97> Save to save\
\
Repeat above for each of the z slices for one fluorescence color then move to next color \
\
To get line to show up on 2nd color have ROI manager open, click on the second colors panel, and then click the line segment name }